{%- comment -%}
  Header blocks as the clients that matter actually write them, with the
  addresses changed. Shared by the tests that read headers.

  Kept apart from the tests themselves, and excluded from the linter in
  .platformos-check.yml, because a header value like
  Message-ID: <001a01dc...> is a real Outlook id and not parseable as
  HTML: the linter reads an angle bracket followed by a digit and stops.
  Weakening the fixture to please it would mean testing mail no client
  sends.
{%- endcomment -%}
